WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.480
20 Years Ago

00:03.060 --> 00:07.920
Yuko and I first met at a church orphanage when we were young.

00:07.920 --> 00:11.610
There were lots of children there who had lost their parents,

00:11.610 --> 00:14.110
and Yuko and I were no exception.

00:15.610 --> 00:19.520
One day, Yuko was adopted and left to go to a new home.

00:19.520 --> 00:22.370
Even after she left, I stayed at the church for a long time.

00:23.000 --> 00:25.830
And that was the only relationship I ever had with Yuko.

00:25.830 --> 00:25.870
Only as for

00:43.640 --> 00:45.670
Onii-chan!

00:47.810 --> 00:50.780
Love, I've got to feel it

00:51.110 --> 00:54.150
If you put your trust in me

00:54.450 --> 00:57.780
I know what my life would be

00:57.780 --> 01:02.580
Oh, you are all I ever need

01:02.750 --> 01:08.290
I try to hear what you say

01:08.420 --> 01:10.550
So I pray

01:10.630 --> 01:14.130
But you're fading away

01:15.550 --> 01:21.310
Don't go and break my fragile heart

01:21.720 --> 01:24.930
We won't fall apart

01:25.020 --> 01:33.110
'Cause you're my only star

01:35.070 --> 01:38.820
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:38.820 --> 01:42.330
Calling you, so like a little child

01:42.490 --> 01:45.540
All the things you have in mind

01:45.830 --> 01:48.920
I wish I could see your insides

01:48.920 --> 01:51.960
My love, you've got to feel it

01:51.960 --> 01:55.260
And if we put our trust in you and me

01:55.470 --> 01:58.930
You know what our lives would be

01:59.050 --> 02:06.890
Oh, you are the one, I believe

02:25.580 --> 02:27.710
I remembered it again.

02:42.260 --> 02:43.050
Now!

02:43.050 --> 02:45.220
Stop by and take a look!

02:45.220 --> 02:47.850
It might not speak to you in this season,

02:47.850 --> 02:51.600
but this sweater is better quality than the ones you see every day.

02:51.600 --> 02:53.190
And how is it different?

02:53.190 --> 02:54.400
Yo, Himura!

02:54.400 --> 02:55.940
You wanna buy this sweater?

02:55.940 --> 02:58.780
I don't want to touch your hand-me-downs.

02:58.780 --> 03:00.530
You're really cold-hearted.

03:00.860 --> 03:04.200
I thought you didn't have to attend school anymore.

03:04.200 --> 03:07.450
I need to sort out some things.

03:07.450 --> 03:08.620
Is it about girls?

03:08.620 --> 03:10.750
That's my top priority, and I've taken care of it already.

03:10.750 --> 03:12.670
That's just like you.

03:13.080 --> 03:15.210
How much is this?

03:16.750 --> 03:18.380
You've really got a good eye for things!

03:18.380 --> 03:19.670
Is it a gift for your boyfriend?

03:19.670 --> 03:21.550
It might be.

03:21.550 --> 03:23.140
Right, Himura-senpai?

03:45.830 --> 03:46.990
Himura-senpai?

03:46.990 --> 03:48.540
What do you want?

03:48.540 --> 03:51.660
I'm not allowed to talk to you unless I want something?

03:51.660 --> 03:55.080
Did you forget already? I told you not to come near me.

03:55.080 --> 03:57.210
I remember precisely.

03:57.210 --> 03:58.090
Then why?

03:58.090 --> 04:01.420
You're free to say whatever you like, Himura-senpai.

04:01.420 --> 04:05.430
But I'm also free to do whatever I like.

04:08.260 --> 04:11.020
Do you mind coming with me for a little while?

04:18.520 --> 04:22.740
Yuko, didn't you say that the Astronomy Club had disbanded?

04:22.740 --> 04:23.700
Yes.

04:23.700 --> 04:26.740
Then why do you have the key to the rooftop?

04:26.740 --> 04:28.160
It's impossible to borrow the key now, isn't it?

04:29.790 --> 04:33.040
The club was boring, but it had a long history.

04:33.040 --> 04:35.710
An upperclassman probably broke the rules sometime in the past.

04:36.250 --> 04:38.040
So he made a copy of the key without permission?

04:38.040 --> 04:41.050
It's been passed down for generations, though.

04:41.050 --> 04:43.880
I received the key when the club disbanded.

04:44.260 --> 04:48.890
Isn't school life more enjoyable when there's a little bit of a thrill?

04:49.220 --> 04:53.350
Unfortunately, I plan to lead a peaceful school life.

04:53.350 --> 04:56.190
Oh? You're really mature.

04:56.190 --> 04:58.730
I can't cause trouble.

04:59.770 --> 05:01.070
Himura-senpai?

05:01.070 --> 05:01.860
What?

05:01.860 --> 05:05.860
Will you tell me some stories about what happened at the orphanage after I left?

05:05.860 --> 05:08.490
Why do you want to know something like that?

05:08.490 --> 05:10.990
I had always lived at the orphanage.

05:10.990 --> 05:14.370
When I was accepted to this school, I finally left the place.

05:14.370 --> 05:15.620
That's all.

05:15.620 --> 05:18.000
You... never left the orphanage?

05:18.330 --> 05:22.050
There wasn't anyone crazy enough to adopt me.

05:22.050 --> 05:28.590
That's why I worked hard, so that I could stop relying on others as quickly as possible.

05:28.590 --> 05:32.140
But... the tuition for Otowa isn't cheap.

05:32.140 --> 05:33.930
I have a scholarship.

05:33.930 --> 05:36.140
I'm exempt from both the entrance fee and tuition.

05:36.140 --> 05:37.900
I didn't want to cause any more trouble.

05:38.850 --> 05:42.070
In order to live in this society, I've been doing various things.

05:43.530 --> 05:44.940
Hey, Yuko...

05:44.940 --> 05:45.860
Yes?

05:45.860 --> 05:47.610
I'll only say it once more.

05:47.610 --> 05:49.160
Don't come near me.

05:50.660 --> 05:53.620
Don't make me remember the past.

05:55.120 --> 05:56.870
Why don't you just forget...

05:57.960 --> 06:01.090
Why don't you just forget about the red watch?

06:02.590 --> 06:04.090
How do you know about...

06:04.090 --> 06:08.090
I knew it. You're still having the same dream.

06:09.090 --> 06:10.590
The

06:26.610 --> 06:28.820
Nice timing.

06:29.740 --> 06:31.820
Good morning, Kuze-san.

06:31.820 --> 06:33.490
Good morning, Mizuki-chan.

06:37.370 --> 06:40.120
Are you sure you don't want to go somewhere?

06:40.120 --> 06:45.590
Since you've just come overseas, isn't it a waste not to do anything special?

06:45.590 --> 06:49.930
You say "overseas", but it's no different from the city of Otowa in Japan!

06:49.930 --> 06:51.140
Well, you're right about that.

06:51.140 --> 06:55.930
Besides, doing laundry with you is definitely something special.

06:55.930 --> 06:57.930
Even on a precious weekend?

06:57.930 --> 07:00.640
Every day is special for me,

07:00.640 --> 07:02.690
whether it's a vacation or not.

07:02.690 --> 07:04.190
You're such a positive thinker.

07:04.190 --> 07:07.280
But isn't it more fun to think of it that way?

07:09.650 --> 07:11.110
Oh, Kuze-san.

07:11.110 --> 07:12.740
Good morning.

07:12.740 --> 07:14.530
Morning, Renji.

07:14.530 --> 07:17.540
Are you making progress on your exam studies?

07:17.540 --> 07:19.910
It's so bad, it's not even funny.

07:19.910 --> 07:20.870
Ah, I see.

07:20.870 --> 07:23.790
Well, despair to your heart's content, young lad.

07:23.790 --> 07:28.050
Anyways, Renji, we're going to do laundry, so gather up the clothes you need washed.

07:28.050 --> 07:30.590
Huh? It's all right. I can do my own laundry.

07:30.590 --> 07:32.720
It's a good opportunity, so go get them anyway.

07:32.720 --> 07:34.220
I said, it's all right!

07:34.220 --> 07:36.970
My mind's all jumbled up with my studies, so leave me alone!

07:39.730 --> 07:44.480
Ah, I see. Well, if you're going to leave it at that, I'll have to take them by force.

07:44.480 --> 07:47.020
Huh? Wait, Mizuki!

07:48.150 --> 07:49.940
I don't care, just take it off!

07:49.940 --> 07:52.240
Quit dawdling and hand it over!

07:54.110 --> 07:56.700
Geez, don't go crazy!

07:57.410 --> 07:59.200
Huh? What's with that towel?

07:59.200 --> 08:01.210
Why are you giving us more laundry?!

08:01.210 --> 08:02.370
Hand that over, too.

08:02.370 --> 08:03.210
No!

08:03.370 --> 08:05.170
Give me a break!

08:05.210 --> 08:06.040
Geez...

08:06.710 --> 08:08.880
He's not a girl or anything.

08:08.880 --> 08:11.130
He doesn't have to start acting shy <i>now!</i>

08:11.130 --> 08:13.380
He's at a sensitive age.

08:13.380 --> 08:16.600
And? What should I help with?

08:16.600 --> 08:18.850
You have to sort out the clothes that could bleed.

08:18.850 --> 08:21.060
I wonder which ones are Sumire-san's underwear.

08:22.140 --> 08:23.770
I separated them already.

08:23.770 --> 08:26.650
Then what in the world did I come here for?

08:28.020 --> 08:30.820
The best part of doing laundry is when you hang it up to dry.

08:30.820 --> 08:36.070
The smell that fills the air as water splashes from the stretched sheets is wonderful!

08:38.910 --> 08:42.790
Kuze-san, why did you start playing the violin?

08:42.790 --> 08:44.370
Let's see...

08:44.370 --> 08:48.790
I think the main catalyst was when I met Johann Mälzel's daughter in the Music Room.

08:48.790 --> 08:50.550
Johann Mälzel's daughter?

08:50.550 --> 08:53.880
She had a dull personality and was very serious.

08:53.880 --> 08:56.550
Yet she was fair towards everybody.

08:56.550 --> 08:59.180
That was my first love.

08:59.180 --> 09:02.180
She taught me many things.

09:02.180 --> 09:06.060
Justice, order, and the toughness of the world.

09:06.060 --> 09:10.360
Eventually, I found out that she was born in 1815.

09:10.360 --> 09:12.690
1815?

09:12.690 --> 09:15.320
Wait, that's almost 200 years ago!

09:15.320 --> 09:18.320
She wasn't your music teacher or something?

09:18.320 --> 09:20.870
To me, she's still my teacher.

09:20.870 --> 09:24.250
Her name is "Metronome".

09:27.670 --> 09:30.250
Oh... geez!

09:30.250 --> 09:31.170
Are you mad?

09:31.170 --> 09:32.710
Do you <i>want me to be?</i>

09:32.710 --> 09:37.130
Heh, you're cuter when you're in a bad mood, Mizuki-chan.

09:37.630 --> 09:39.140
Wh-What?!

09:40.640 --> 09:43.020
Th-The washing is done.

09:43.020 --> 09:45.140
I'm going to hang it now, so please help me.

09:54.030 --> 09:55.650
Kuze-san?! Kuze-san?!

09:55.650 --> 09:57.530
What happened?!

09:57.530 --> 09:58.950
An ambulance, an ambulance!

10:01.370 --> 10:04.080
Geez, why isn't the call going through?!

10:08.920 --> 10:10.750
Sumire-san...

10:14.250 --> 10:18.130
I guess I can't leave him like this.

10:31.690 --> 10:33.820
Well, I didn't mean any harm.

10:36.190 --> 10:38.450
I hope this is okay.

10:51.880 --> 10:53.000
Kuze-san?

10:54.550 --> 10:57.050
Kuze-san, are you all right?

10:57.050 --> 10:59.550
As long as an angel keeps smiling at me...

11:00.590 --> 11:02.680
Yep, seems like you're all right.

11:03.140 --> 11:04.300
Is this a dream?

11:04.300 --> 11:06.180
Dunno. What do you think?

11:07.180 --> 11:08.350
I can't sleep.

11:08.350 --> 11:09.140
Huh?

11:09.140 --> 11:11.940
When I'm by myself, I get bad dreams.

11:14.520 --> 11:15.940
It's all right,

11:15.940 --> 11:17.690
because I'm here.

11:20.820 --> 11:22.410
Good night.

11:23.320 --> 11:25.330
for

11:29.410 --> 11:30.750
Huh?

11:30.750 --> 11:33.170
Why am I...

11:33.170 --> 11:35.380
Ah! Kuze-san, are you awake?

11:35.380 --> 11:37.960
Mizuki-chan, was I asleep?

11:37.960 --> 11:39.840
Yep, sleeping soundly!

11:43.180 --> 11:44.800
Sorry about that, Mizuki-chan.

11:44.800 --> 11:46.680
Your whole day has gone to waste.

11:46.680 --> 11:48.100
Oh, it's okay!

11:48.100 --> 11:52.060
I like to spend a leisurely day like this every now and then.

11:52.060 --> 11:55.020
I'll make up for it tomorrow.

11:55.020 --> 11:55.980
I look forward to it.

12:00.400 --> 12:02.240
What's that?

12:02.240 --> 12:04.410
Nah, nothing.

12:16.340 --> 12:17.750
What are you doing?

12:18.130 --> 12:20.420
Just a clean break from my sweet memories.

12:21.720 --> 12:23.760
Are those from girls you've dated?

12:23.760 --> 12:26.090
They came back because the recipient was unknown.

12:26.090 --> 12:28.970
She probably sold the place where she used to live.

12:28.970 --> 12:30.180
Are you okay with that?

12:30.180 --> 12:32.270
What, are you saying that there's another option?

12:32.520 --> 12:37.060
I thought everything was solved, but why did these come back to me?

12:37.060 --> 12:39.320
They make me remember the past.

12:39.650 --> 12:42.990
And worse yet, it happened at a time like this.

12:42.990 --> 12:43.950
A time like this?

12:43.950 --> 12:46.280
No, it's nothing.

12:46.280 --> 12:50.240
So I guess her letters aren't the only things that came back.

12:50.240 --> 12:53.540
I got rid of all my troublesome interpersonal relationships,

12:53.540 --> 12:55.420
but why is this happening <i>now?</i>

12:55.420 --> 12:56.790
Whoa! This is a rare one.

12:56.790 --> 12:58.670
Hirono Nagi.

12:58.670 --> 12:59.880
I wonder if she's well.

12:59.880 --> 13:01.510
What did she say?

13:01.510 --> 13:03.260
Who knows?

13:05.130 --> 13:07.760
And? What do you plan to do now?

13:09.140 --> 13:10.560
It's obvious, isn't it?

13:13.890 --> 13:15.560
I'll throw them all away.

13:15.560 --> 13:16.980
That's all.

13:16.980 --> 13:20.480
The wounded heart is being healed

13:16.980 --> 13:20.480
I heard a gentle sound

13:33.000 --> 13:34.250
Akane.

13:35.910 --> 13:37.750
Onii-chan!

13:40.920 --> 13:42.340
Onii-chan!

13:43.340 --> 13:44.460
Akane?!

13:45.510 --> 13:47.050
Let's play!

13:50.050 --> 13:52.470
Onii-chan, what's wrong?

13:53.560 --> 13:54.810
Onii-chan?

13:54.810 --> 13:56.810
Onii-chan!

14:00.940 --> 14:05.280
Ah! You're so good at drawing, Yu onii-chan!

14:05.280 --> 14:07.530
Stop calling me "onii-chan!"

14:07.530 --> 14:08.700
Why?

14:08.700 --> 14:10.160
Just because!

14:10.160 --> 14:11.910
I'm not your brother!

14:12.950 --> 14:15.290
Then... what am I supposed to call you?

14:15.290 --> 14:17.250
Like I'd know!

14:17.250 --> 14:19.710
Then... Yu-kun...

14:21.710 --> 14:24.550
Yu-kun, do you like art?

14:24.550 --> 14:25.670
I guess.

14:26.720 --> 14:28.840
Yu-kun, you're really good at it!

14:28.840 --> 14:30.180
I guess.

14:30.180 --> 14:31.850
What do you want?

14:31.850 --> 14:32.800
Yu-kun!

14:32.800 --> 14:34.720
Yeah, so what do you want?

14:34.720 --> 14:36.180
Nothing!

14:41.100 --> 14:44.070
Hey Yu-kun, will you draw me next?

14:44.070 --> 14:44.900
Huh?

14:44.900 --> 14:45.980
Draw me!

14:45.980 --> 14:47.650
Fine, I guess...

14:54.030 --> 14:56.200
What's wrong?

14:56.200 --> 14:57.500
I've decided not to.

14:57.500 --> 14:58.660
How come?

14:58.660 --> 15:00.290
It's a waste of paper.

15:00.290 --> 15:01.170
That's cruel!

15:01.170 --> 15:02.920
Yu-kun, you're so stingy!

15:02.920 --> 15:04.420
I really don't have much paper left.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.880
Oh, I see...

15:06.880 --> 15:08.170
Well, then it's fine.

15:08.170 --> 15:10.760
Whoa, you gave up pretty quickly.

15:10.760 --> 15:15.100
And in return for that, you have to show me all the pictures you draw, okay?

15:15.100 --> 15:18.230
Because I want to see everything you draw!

15:18.230 --> 15:19.310
Sure.

16:02.270 --> 16:03.350
Yu-kun!

16:03.350 --> 16:04.150
What?

16:04.150 --> 16:07.360
Yu-kun... you don't need a sister?

16:08.820 --> 16:12.070
I mean... you don't want a sister?

16:12.070 --> 16:14.910
Why... are you asking me something like that?

16:15.410 --> 16:17.120
Just because.

16:18.740 --> 16:20.120
Yu-kun...

16:22.250 --> 16:23.670
Yu-kun?

16:24.620 --> 16:25.580
I don't...

16:28.340 --> 16:29.750
I don't need a sister anymore.

16:30.840 --> 16:33.800
I... can't take it anymore.

16:33.800 --> 16:34.930
Yu onii-chan!

16:34.930 --> 16:36.260
Don't call me "onii-chan!"

16:38.180 --> 16:41.140
My sister... died.

16:43.310 --> 16:45.060
Right. I got it.

16:50.070 --> 16:51.820
A few days later,

16:51.820 --> 16:54.400
Yuko was adopted by some distant relatives,

16:54.400 --> 16:55.990
and left the orphanage.

17:14.470 --> 17:17.840
People... are always alone in the end.

17:18.640 --> 17:21.430
Whether they're related or not,

17:21.430 --> 17:24.640
someday, they'll be separated.

17:25.600 --> 17:29.610
That's why I don't expect anything from others.

17:29.610 --> 17:33.440
That's why I don't interfere with others.

17:33.440 --> 17:37.700
That's why I've learned to live without relying on others.

17:48.750 --> 17:53.090
And despite all that, why do you continue to follow me around?

17:53.090 --> 17:55.220
Hm, I wonder why?

17:56.550 --> 18:00.680
Senpai, I'm happy that I was able to see you again.

18:00.680 --> 18:02.350
Do you understand why?

18:02.350 --> 18:03.560
Who knows?

18:03.560 --> 18:05.600
You're so slow, Senpai.

18:05.600 --> 18:08.190
Just as always.

18:08.190 --> 18:10.020
Are you trying to pick a fight?

18:10.020 --> 18:12.070
I guess I'm left with no other option.

18:12.070 --> 18:13.980
So I'll tell you why.

18:13.980 --> 18:16.360
Himura-senpai...

18:16.360 --> 18:19.490
you were my first love.

18:21.120 --> 18:26.580
My first love hasn't ended yet, Yu-kun.

18:30.630 --> 18:32.250
I'll make you forget.

18:34.250 --> 18:38.220
I'll erase all of your sad memories.

18:58.570 --> 18:59.990
Heart rate, 60.

18:59.990 --> 19:01.070
Optimal range.

19:03.330 --> 19:04.830
MM 60.

19:04.830 --> 19:05.540
Largo.

19:10.370 --> 19:13.670
Normal synchronization, all status clear.

19:13.670 --> 19:15.550
Widely, and moderately.

19:19.800 --> 19:22.930
Kuze-kun, you were a bit late there.

19:22.930 --> 19:24.350
Yeah, it was sloppy.

19:24.930 --> 19:28.850
Is your metronome really a musician's heart?

19:29.230 --> 19:33.610
Is your heart really a musician's metronome?

19:38.030 --> 19:40.740
The Zenmai spring is going to uncoil soon.

19:40.740 --> 19:42.910
And who's going to coil it up again?

19:47.450 --> 19:50.830
The ticking rhythm is the time remaining.

19:53.830 --> 19:54.960
Kuze-san!

19:56.880 --> 19:58.380
Mizuki-chan.

19:58.380 --> 20:00.010
What's up at a time like this?

20:00.880 --> 20:04.050
I couldn't really sleep, so I came out here to cool off.

20:04.050 --> 20:05.890
I see.

20:05.890 --> 20:07.600
Ah, Kuze-san! That's...

20:08.850 --> 20:11.430
Did you get it repaired?

20:11.430 --> 20:12.690
Repaired?

20:12.690 --> 20:15.860
Oh! Um... sorry, it's still not fixed yet.

20:15.860 --> 20:18.900
Oh... I see.

20:18.900 --> 20:20.110
Bummer.

20:20.110 --> 20:21.400
Yup.

20:21.400 --> 20:23.610
It's never going to work again.

20:25.120 --> 20:29.040
I listened to the CD you gave me.

20:29.040 --> 20:33.620
Since I've rarely listened to classical music before, it was amazing!

20:33.620 --> 20:36.540
A quiet piece is really pleasant,

20:36.540 --> 20:39.670
and there are also some pieces that suddenly go <i>boom, aren't there?</i>

20:39.670 --> 20:42.170
It was so cool, my back trembled!

20:42.170 --> 20:43.130
<i>Boom?</i>

20:43.130 --> 20:46.300
But the thing that surprised me the most

20:46.300 --> 20:49.680
is that classical music turns out to be really sexy.

20:49.680 --> 20:50.930
Sexy?

20:50.930 --> 20:53.140
There are no lyrics or anything,

20:53.140 --> 20:56.270
but it's as if someone is by your side, whispering in your ear.

20:56.270 --> 21:00.690
It's as if they're whispering, "I love you".

21:00.690 --> 21:02.530
It really made my heart pound.

21:02.530 --> 21:03.740
Well, they <i>do say</i>

21:03.740 --> 21:07.530
that the most famous songs are written while in love or suffering from heartbreak.

21:08.160 --> 21:14.410
When I was thinking about that, I began to feel something for you, as the performer of the piece...

21:14.410 --> 21:15.460
Huh?

21:15.460 --> 21:17.830
Kuze-san, this is really sudden, but...

21:17.830 --> 21:18.710
What?

21:21.590 --> 21:24.720
I think... I've fallen in love with you!

21:26.630 --> 21:28.470
Well then, see you tomorrow!

21:43.230 --> 21:45.070
Man, I'm beat.

22:09.430 --> 22:15.850
hikaru kaze odayaka ni

22:09.430 --> 22:22.820
The shining wind calmly sways from gaps in the clouds.

22:23.440 --> 22:30.240
The echoing sounds sparkle.

22:30.410 --> 22:33.740
Even if it's a hope that was nearly lost,

22:33.990 --> 22:41.380
I should be able to find it again

22:43.670 --> 22:46.590
Holding firmly onto your sound,

22:47.170 --> 22:56.770
I don't let go of your hand joined with mine.

22:57.680 --> 23:03.520
Please don't forget the important things.

23:04.690 --> 23:11.200
A smile continues on into the future.

23:26.050 --> 23:28.130
The facade is that of a clown.

23:28.130 --> 23:30.630
The hidden emotion is gaudiness.

23:30.630 --> 23:33.430
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:33.430 --> 23:35.220
Union.

23:35.220 --> 23:38.060
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
